## [ISSUE] One failed cancel stops all the remaining cancels in the cron run

**Severity:** MEDIUM — one bad batch (or hitting the 100-pending-cancellation limit) stops every other cancelled reminder in the same run from being cancelled.

### The Problem
```ts
try {
  const workflowRemindersToDelete = [];
  for (const reminder of remindersToCancel) {
    await client.request({ url: "/v3/user/scheduled_sends", method: "POST", body: {...} });
    const workflowReminderToDelete = prisma.workflowReminder.delete({ where: { id: reminder.id } });
    workflowRemindersToDelete.push(workflowReminderToDelete);
  }
  await Promise.all(workflowRemindersToDelete);
} catch (error) {
  console.log(`Error cancelling scheduled Emails: ${error}`);
}
```

### Theory / Proof
- If `client.request` throws for reminder N (SendGrid 4xx/5xx, the 100-pending limit this PR describes, a network error), the code jumps to `catch`. Reminders N+1..end are not cancelled in this run.
- Prisma query builders (`PrismaPromise`) are lazy and only run when `.then()` is called (Prisma docs, "PrismaPromise ... queries are only executed when awaited"). The deletes for reminders 1..N-1 were pushed but never awaited, so they never run. Those rows stay `cancelled: true` and get POSTed again on the next run.
- `findMany` has no `orderBy`, but Postgres usually returns the rows in a stable order. A reminder that keeps failing therefore tends to block the same set of later reminders on every run until its `scheduledDate` passes and the cleanup at line 34 deletes it. That can take up to an hour, and during that hour the emails for the blocked reminders go out.

### What happens today vs. what will break
When every request succeeds, this works. It breaks on the first error, which is exactly the situation (SendGrid rejecting cancels) that caused #7225.

### Research
Every other loop in this file isolates failures per item. For example, the scheduling loop below wraps each reminder in its own `try` (`for (const reminder of unscheduledReminders) { try { ... } catch ... }`).

### Recommendation
Handle errors per reminder, and only delete the row after its cancel succeeds:

```ts
for (const reminder of remindersToCancel) {
  try {
    await client.request({ url: "/v3/user/scheduled_sends", method: "POST",
      body: { batch_id: reminder.referenceId, status: "cancel" } });
    await prisma.workflowReminder.delete({ where: { id: reminder.id } });
  } catch (error) {
    console.log(`Error cancelling scheduled email ${reminder.id}: ${error}`);
  }
}
```
